6.9 Referential Integrity
The database enforces the following referential integrity constraints:

Every scale_relation.scale_id and scale_relation.related_scale_id must exist in scale.

Every stag_link.scale_id must exist in scale.

Every verification_link.scale_id must exist in scale.

Every work_link.scale_id must exist in scale.

Every provenance.scale_id must exist in scale.

Every moderation.scale_id must exist in scale.

The version chain (supersedes and superseded_by) must be acyclic.

The scale-relation relation must be symmetric where appropriate: if A is above B, B must be below A; if A is adjacent to B, B must be adjacent to A.

