Validation Engine Design
The atlas validates the following:

Validation 1. Scale validity. Every scale is validated against the scale schema before it is stored.

Validation 2. STAG annotation validity. Every STAG annotation is validated against the STAG schema and the thirty-two semantic rules.

Validation 3. Numerical verification result validity. Every numerical verification result is validated against the verification schema.

Validation 4. Referential integrity. Every foreign key reference must resolve to an existing record.

Validation 5. Version chain acyclicity. The version chain must be acyclic.

Validation 6. Scale-relation symmetry. The scale-relation relation must be symmetric where appropriate.

Validation 7. Work resolution. Every work_reference must resolve to a work in the Physics Knowledge Library, or be flagged as unresolved.

Validation 8. Provenance completeness. Every scale must have a provenance record.

Validation 9. Audit completeness. Every operation must have an audit log entry.

Validation 10. Moderation completeness. Every scale must have a moderation record.

Validation 11. Order-of-magnitude consistency. The order_of_magnitude must be consistent with the scale_value.

